--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- range graph and touchdown point of a surging chain in waves, 120 s
-- Studless chain in 50 m of water, End B anchored 400 m from the fairlead. The fairlead surges
-- 5 m at a 30 s period (motionFile, 15 s smooth start) under a regular Airy wave (H = 6 m,
-- T = 10 s, 10 s ramp). The LINES Outputs flag r writes the range graph <root>.Line1.range.out:
-- the minimum, maximum and mean over t >= RangeStart of the node tension, curvature, bend
-- moment, declination and seabed clearance. The TDP1 channels track the touchdown point: arc
-- length from the fairlead, position, layback, and excursion from the static touchdown point.
-- Plot the tension envelope with plot_range_envelope.py.
